# Steamworks: Stats and achievements

Every SetAchievement/SetStat needs a StoreStats afterwards or nothing reaches Steam. Use exactly the API names defined in Steamworks (steamworks.yaml lists them); a typo fails silently.

## Achievements or stats are set but never stored (error)

- Why: SetAchievement and SetStat only change the local copy; nothing reaches Steam until StoreStats is called.
- Fix: Call StoreStats after setting achievements or stats (SteamUserStats.StoreStats(), Steam.storeStats()).
- Source: https://partner.steamgames.com/doc/features/achievements

## The code uses an achievement that is not defined (error)

- Why: Steam ignores an API name it does not know, so the achievement can never be unlocked.
- Fix: Use an API name from steamworks.yaml, or add the achievement there (and to Steamworks).
- Source: https://partner.steamgames.com/doc/features/achievements

## The code uses a stat that is not defined (warning)

- Why: Steam ignores a stat API name it does not know.
- Fix: Use a stat name from steamworks.yaml (stats), or add the stat there and in Steamworks.
- Source: https://partner.steamgames.com/doc/features/achievements

## An achievement is defined but no code unlocks it (info)

- Why: Players see it on the store and in the library but can never earn it.
- Fix: Unlock it in code, or remove it before release. (Achievements unlocked through a stat's progress are fine.)
- Source: https://partner.steamgames.com/doc/features/achievements

With the steamworks-mcp server connected, `check_code(path)` finds these problems in the whole project, with file and line (`check_code(path, rules=["steamworks-stats-achievements"])` for this group only).
